iews these are  violations of free speech and really  going off the deep end with  this stuff the bottom line here is I  hate to break it to you but this really  isn't very controversial we might not  like it we might disagree with these  policies but YouTube has Terms of  Service guidelines the David Pakman show  has had videos demonetised we've had  videos flagged as age restricted that I  didn't necessarily agree should be age  restricted which limits the amount of  money you can make on them we've had  videos removed altogether although not  for content but because of for example  alleged copyright infringement it's not  a political attack on the David Pakman  show it's part of the sort of anti  controversy bias that YouTube has  because of its advertiser relationships  Facebook some of our content has been  flagged on Facebook because we had  b-roll right that video that sometimes  plays while I'm describing the story to  you if that was allegedly too graphic or  exceeded sort of went over the line that  Facebook has set for its community I  don't like it it's just not a huge deal  and I wish the policy were different I  wish I could always monetize every  single video and get you know a hundred  percent of the possible revenue out of  the content we produce as opposed to  some fraction short of a hundred percent  but the framing of this entire thing as  an anti Alex Jones conspiracy is just  totally without evidence and the problem  with Jones's he builds up a narrative of  the globalist are controlling the media  and they're hiding the truth and they  want to censor me or him as Alex Jones  would say then a few of his episodes get  removed and now that becomes evidence  supposedly supporting that conspiracy  theory it's sort of like the if I said  car companies set up brakes to need to  be replaced all the time so that you  have to spend money imagine that I say  that every single day on the show car  companies are running a scam that is  break pads they're running a scam and  after 18 months my brake pads now have  actually worn out and I finally have to  change them and I say look this is proof  that my conspiracy theory it is accurate  I've been saying this for 18 months is  it really or is it  just that after 18 months at some point  you got to replace your brake pads and  Spotify and YouTube and Facebook have no  obligation to host Alex Jones content if  he wants to run his own servers he can  put whatever the hell he wants on those  servers and there won't be anybody there  who could even possibly censor him  assuming the content isn't illegal but  that would be him saying well I want a  forgo the audience that YouTube brings  or the audience that Facebook brings and  put the content on my own server  the real concern here is not a few  episodes getting removed  it's that Alex Jones and Trump and  others are all participating in what I  call the degradation of political  discourse the types of conversations and  this is why I've talked about we will  sometimes in a tongue-in-cheek away use  the word cuck but it's really to kind of  make fun of the people that use it and  I've said I I don't know if that's a  good idea because even using the term  sarcastically suggests that it might  even be a valid term in political  discourse Jones and Trump and these  others have either under the name of  telling it like it is or telling a truth  that nobody else is willing to or  whatever it fuels this reduction of  politics to bottom-feeding sort of  lowest-common-denominator debate and  conspiracy theories and not having to  defend what you say with any kind of  facts that's what's really dangerous and  the entire sort of milieu that considers  this even remotely reasonable debate  what Alex Jones does the comet ping-pong  thing which I guess he's backed off of  now at this point whether you believe  eight of ten facts or six of ten  assertions or whatever about comet  ping-pong the idea that that entire  story even qualifie